{"kind":"assert","text":"H3 Order 1 rulings, from section 5.3 of notes/2026-10-18-sequenced-level-and-order-scope.md.\n\n1. Retry after resolution: a repeat allocate for the same (member, input) whose allocation is resolved returns that allocation's fact at the same position. It never opens a new position. A resolved position has a determined result, and a second position would let one input commit twice. Only holed and expired allocations open a new position on repeat, as the note says. Keep the bounded terminal position and the input evidence you drafted, so the match survives after the payload falls below the floor.\n\n2. Lifetime range: 60 to 86,400 seconds, inclusive. Genesis refuses any value outside that range, and the package check refuses the same range. The floor of 60 s stays above the fetch limit and one attention tick. The ceiling of one day bounds how long a reader can wait on an undetermined position.\n\n3. Future position: refuse it with not-open. A position beyond the order journal names no allocation. That is a deterministic answer from the authoritative journal, not a transient one. unavailable stays reserved for no answer within the limit.\n\n4. Expiry attention goes to the allocation's own member, the MemberRef recorded at enroll for the member field. The creator does not receive it. That member holds the pending row and must hole it or resume.\n\nH5 owner: request f3138ddd. This act adds two items to its work: general admission of referenced definitions in create sends (not Order alone), and both installed Order lineage cases from your archived witness f6dfae8b. The H3 Status names f3138ddd for the installed pair.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}